1. OAI/  (478 files)
   From OpenAI's mathematics repository, https://github.com/openai/math,
   commit fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb, directory lean/OAI/
   (the formalization accompanying "Catalan's constant is irrational", OpenAI, 2026).
   Only the files needed by this development are included. They were modified as follows:
   - each file was mechanically converted to Lean's module system (a `module` header,
     `public import`, and `@[expose] public section` after the imports);
   - minimal changes were made for Lean v4.35.0-rc2 and Mathlib v4.35.0-rc2 (see PORTING.md);
   - in the 37 point-evaluation files OAI/NumberTheory/Catalan/SecondBarrier/
     BarrierCaseTwoPoint{X0..X18,Y0..Y17}.lean and in BarrierCaseTwoGlobalBounds.lean, the
     comparison constants -98399/100000 and -160890/100000 were replaced by the sharper
     -9840333/10000000 and -16089463/10000000; the evaluation points and rational
     approximations are unchanged, and BarrierCaseTwoGlobalBounds.lean keeps OpenAI's original
     statements as corollaries (barrierCase2X_global_upper, barrierCase2Y_global_upper).
   Apart from these sharpened constants, the mathematical content and the declarations are
   unchanged.

2. PrimeNumberTheoremAnd/  (10 files)
   Files that OpenAI's repository adds to the PrimeNumberTheoremAnd project
   (https://github.com/AlexKontorovich/PrimeNumberTheoremAnd, commit
   c39a751132c88b6e8080b74c74023fd95b3d8be0) through its compatibility patch
   lean/patches/PrimeNumberTheoremAnd-lean4341.patch at the commit above.
   They were modified in the same way as item 1.

3. scripts/, test/, docbuild/, .github/, Gemfile, Gemfile.lock
   From the Palomar submission template, https://github.com/PalomarRegistry/PalomarTemplate,
   adapted to this project.

4. CatalanMeasure/GenD/Signed/Davis/ and archive/CatalanArchive/GenD/Signed/Davis/
   (33 files listed in PROVENANCE.json in the first directory)
   From Cinna Davis's formalization, https://github.com/1337isnot1337/catalan-constant,
   commit 3c4515314bda407d032cb55f60bfc56b03c1d3f9, under the Apache License 2.0. Two files,
   GeneralNodalWeights.lean and NodalRootDeletion.lean (weight bounds for a nodal polynomial
   family), are used by the proof. The other 31, the inverse-image quadrature nodes and their
   finite branch certificates, are kept in the archive directory and are not part of the build.
   The files were moved to the module path CatalanMeasure.GenD.Signed.Davis; their declaration
   namespaces and proofs are unchanged. Source paths and hashes are in PROVENANCE.json and the original notice in
   NOTICE in that directory. The other files of that directory are new work.

5. CatalanCore/Zeta5/Port/
   From Moritz Firsching's formalization of the irrationality of zeta(5),
   https://github.com/mo271/Zeta5, commit 7fe736760f4b96bfdb4334b68e3b3124ecbe10b0, directory Apery/,
   under the Apache License 2.0. Adapted files: Zeta5.lean, Construction.lean, Degree.lean, Weight.lean,
   Moments.lean, PartialFractions.lean, Hermite.lean, HermiteIntegrals.lean, HermiteIBP.lean,
   HermiteFormula.lean, Positivity.lean, Andreief.lean, DetIntegral.lean, and the declarations
   padicValNat_finset_prod and S_eq_div of Legendre.lean. Modifications: conversion to the Lean module
   system; `import Mathlib` replaced by explicit Mathlib imports and Apery.* renamed to
   CatalanCore.Zeta5.Port.*; in Positivity.lean the positive-definiteness argument of Δ_pos is separated
   into the lemmas gram_quadForm and G_posDef; Legendre.lean reduced to the two declarations above.
   SourceFacts.lean and Source.lean in that directory are new work. Each adapted file carries a header
   line naming its source file and changes.

Everything else (CatalanMeasure/ apart from item 4, CatalanCore/Zeta5/ apart from item 5, CatalanMeasure.lean, Challenge.lean, Solution.lean,
ChallengeZeta5.lean, SolutionZeta5.lean, ChallengeLai.lean, SolutionLai.lean, CatalanCore/Lai/,
comparator.json, comparator-zeta5.json, comparator-lai.json, formalization.yaml, formalization-zeta5.yaml,
formalization-lai.yaml, README.md, PORTING.md, paper/, paper-zeta5/, paper-lai/, scripts/certgen/) is new work
for this project.

The general determinant lemmas and first-case dual bound were later moved, with unchanged
statements and proof bodies, from RealDeterminantUpper.lean into the new vendored file
OAI/NumberTheory/Catalan/Determinants/RealDeterminantCore.lean. Two generic denominator
lemmas from OpenAI's Case2Height namespace were also copied, with unchanged proof bodies,
into CatalanMeasure/Cert/DenominatorBounds.lean. These changes isolate reusable lemmas from
the old second-case certificate, which the current main proof supersedes.
